// EXPECT: [E086]
// Overflow prove-or-reject now covers usize/isize: `x - 1` at x = 0 underflows
// the unsigned type to SIZE_MAX. Previously parse_iN_uN did not recognize
// `usize`, so type_integer_range returned "no range" and EVERY overflow/
// underflow check on usize was silently skipped. Now usize carries a range
// (lower bound 0), so the sub-zero result is rejected.
//
// (The `extern` below is not decoration: without it the program's FIRST error is an undeclared
// `libc_printf`, and that only stayed hidden because the legacy overflow check fired on line 9
// before the resolver reached line 11. Once the sovereign engine owned the obligation, the test
// started asserting its subject by accident of ordering — so the declaration is stated and the
// underflow is what the test is about.)
extern proc libc_printf(fmt *u8, ...) i32
func main() i32 effects io {
    var x usize = 0
    var y usize = x - 1
    libc_printf("%zu\n", y)
    return 0
}
